			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodule — Output Tauri 2 fix, Sky extensions refresh\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 2c5e3233, integrating command-name fixes in Output and live Extensions view refresh in Sky.\n\nOutput renames four Shared Process health-check commands from PascalCase (`CocoonExtensionHostHealth`, `CocoonSearchServiceHealth`, `CocoonDebugServiceHealth`, `SharedProcessServiceHealth`) to snake_case to match Mountain's registered Tauri 2 handler names. Tauri 2 passes the literal Rust function name as the command identifier without the auto-camel conversion present in Tauri 1, so the previously mismatched names caused runtime `Command not found` errors for all per-service health probes.\n\nSky adds `RefreshExtensionsView`, a guard that programmatically calls `workbench.extensions.action.refreshExtension` via `Commands.executeCommand` after Mountain emits `extensions:install` (VsixInstaller success) or `extensions:uninstall`. VS Code's `IExtensionGalleryService` install pipeline exposes no public hook accessible from outside Cocoon's process boundary, so the command is invoked with a try/catch wrapper preventing DOM CustomEvent dispatch failures from disrupting Wind orchestration listeners. The Extensions sidebar now reflects newly installed or removed extensions live without requiring a workbench reload.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application root — pure submodule pointer update.",
			"SHA": "8ae749d3c9080cd51220c3e72ef26eb996eaa3a3"
		},
