				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Dependency and Element submodule pointers\n\nAdvance the Dependency submodule (e481e786 → 47a63f93) and Element submodule (d223e6fd → 0f281e45) to integrate upstream improvements across the dependency tree and editor component layer.\n\nDependency (Deps/Editor): Incorporates Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency advances including a grid-based sessions UI for the Cocoon extension host, SSH encrypted private key passphrase support for Mountain-to-Cocoon remote agent host connectivity, worktree timeout hardening (30s → 60s), and remote session resilience fixes.\n\nElement: Integrates a refactor of Output's InjectTauriDragRegion from a runtime WKWebView stylesheet walker to a build-time CSS source scanner, Wind daily codegen regeneration (CommandCatalog 551→550, ServiceCatalog 500→502), Cocoon Target artifact rebuild, and Mountain CI dependency bump (ad-m/github-push-action 1.1.0 → 1.3.0).\n\nNo source changes in the Land application root — pure submodule pointer updates.",
			"SHA": "7dd94c1c2368fba2d9a05944902ecc27a26dab85"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T14:18:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Advance Element — stylesheet-driven drag selectors\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to d223e6fd, integrating a refactor of the Output component that eliminates the brittle hardcoded titlebar-drag selector list in InjectTauriDragRegion.\n\nThe polyfill now walks the document's stylesheets at runtime to discover which elements VS Code already declares as -webkit-app-region: drag/no-drag in its CSS rules, and stamps the equivalent data-tauri-drag-region attribute dynamically. The walker recurses into CSSMediaRule and CSSSupportsRule containers for OS-scoped and feature-gated rules, caches selectors after the first pass, runs a second collection on window.onload for lazy-loaded extension sheets, and skips cross-origin stylesheets defensively with per-selector error isolation.\n\nThis eliminates manual polyfill maintenance when VS Code upstream changes its titlebar or sidebar markup — the drag regions now reflect whatever the stylesheets declare.",
			"SHA": "1950dc41a704c93851209d41c1566966965999b5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T14:04:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				144,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodule — Mountain name revert, Output UI polyfills, Wind regeneration\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to e966e663, integrating three parallel workstreams across Mountain, Output, and Wind.\n\nMountain reverts the binary, library, and package names from the verbose encoded build-configuration string back to the canonical \"Mountain\", reducing friction in local debugging and tooling. The Tauri identifier is restored to fiddee.editor.binary, resource entries are reordered for consistency, and the missing shell-integration/zsh.zsh resource is added.\n\nOutput introduces two Tauri 2 editor UI polyfills: InjectTauriDragRegion stamps data-tauri-drag-region attributes on titlebar elements so native window-drag hit-testing works with the overlay-titlebar configuration, and MacTitlebarOffsetCSS gains a triple-signal fullscreen detector (HTML5 Fullscreen API, display-mode media query, dimension heuristic) to reclaim 80px left padding when macOS native fullscreen hides the traffic-light cluster. InjectPartZIndexCSS is gated behind DisableUIFixes to prevent menubar and dropdown clipping.\n\nWind regenerates the full set of generated artifacts — CommandCatalog (551 entries), ServiceCatalog (500 entries), per-service Upstream interfaces for ~500 services, and 16 bridge shapes — all carrying the DO NOT EDIT BY HAND header.",
			"SHA": "355753b2b07ea0d894fb4bfb64f91203acb4791c"
		},
